# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# opensidian — binary .deb control template (Debian 13 / Ubuntu 26.04).
# Filled in by bin/hz/deb-build.sh (harness): @VERSION@, @INSTALLED_SIZE@ and
# @DEPENDS@. Depends is NOT written by hand: it is dpkg-shlibdeps' shlibs:Depends
# for the wrapped release binary (DT_NEEDED -> libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0, libgtk-3-0t64, ...).
# Comment lines (#) are stripped before the file becomes DEBIAN/control.
Package: opensidian
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: jpzk <jendrik@madewithtea.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: editors
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/jpzk/opensidian
Description: Local-first markdown vault editor
 opensidian is a local-first markdown editor for a folder of plain files (a
 vault): tabbed editing, wiki links, a graph view and custom themes. It keeps
 your notes as files on disk and never needs a network connection.
